************** G E N E R A L   I N F O R M A T I O N *************4728 1451   22
                                                                  4728 1451   23
This evaluated data file is based on a software system built      4728 1451   24
around the nuclear model code TALYS [kon07], version 2.0. It is   4728 1451   25
part of a large collection of isotopic evaluations, all created by4728 1451   26
running the system with either adjusted or default input          4728 1451   27
parameters. This means that the data in the entire collection have4728 1451   28
been tested in detail for many isotopes against individual        4728 1451   29
experimental data, while for other isotopes it is only as good as 4728 1451   30
the global quality of TALYS at the moment. The mutual quality of  4728 1451   31
all individual data files is however consistent: The same set of  4728 1451   32
nuclear models is used and, equally important, the same ENDF-6    4728 1451   33
formatting procedures for each isotope. The data file has been    4728 1451   34
created automatically using the ENDF-6 format generator TEFAL.    4728 1451   35
                                                                  4728 1451   36
The resulting data file provides a complete representation of     4728 1451   37
nuclear data needed for transport, activation, damage, heating,   4728 1451   38
radioactivity, and shielding applications over the incident       4728 1451   39
proton energy range from 0.25 to 200. MeV.                        4728 1451   40
                                                                  4728 1451   41
All transport and activation data for neutrons, charged particles,4728 1451   42
photons and residual nuclides are filed. This includes cross      4728 1451   43
sections, angular distributions, double-differential spectra,     4728 1451   44
isomeric production, discrete and continuum photon production     4728 1451   45
cross sections, residual production cross sections and recoils.   4728 1451   46
This general purpose evaluation can thus be used as both          4728 1451   47
transport and activation library.                                 4728 1451   48
                                                                  4728 1451   49
A complete set of covariance data is included, which is stored    4728 1451   50
in MF31-40.                                                       4728 1451   51
                                                                  4728 1451   52
**** N U C L I D E    S P E C I F I C   I N F O R M A T I O N ****4728 1451   53
                                                                  4728 1451   54
None                                                              4728 1451   55
                                                                  4728 1451   56
***************************** T A L Y S **************************4728 1451   57
                                                                  4728 1451   58
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   4728 1451   59
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      4728 1451   60
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    4728 1451   61
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     4728 1451   62
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  4728 1451   63
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        4728 1451   64
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    4728 1451   65
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         4728 1451   66
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      4728 1451   67
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    4728 1451   68
stored in this data file:                                         4728 1451   69
                                                                  4728 1451   70
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   4728 1451   71
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     4728 1451   72
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 4728 1451   73
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   4728 1451   74
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                4728 1451   75
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   4728 1451   76
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    4728 1451   77
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        4728 1451   78
- Recoil data                                                     4728 1451   79
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (p,xn), (p,xp),..           4728 1451   80
- Total particle energy spectra                                   4728 1451   81
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      4728 1451   82
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        4728 1451   83
- Residual production cross sections                              4728 1451   84
                                                                  4728 1451   85
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            4728 1451   86
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        4728 1451   87
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   4728 1451   88
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                4728 1451   89
                                                                  4728 1451   90
