                                                                  4728 1451   92
##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    4728 1451   93
                                                                  4728 1451   94
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       4728 1451   95
                                                                  4728 1451   96
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          4728 1451   97
                                                                  4728 1451   98
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                4728 1451   99
                                                                  4728 1451  100
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       4728 1451  101
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  4728 1451  102
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   4728 1451  103
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  4728 1451  104
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  4728 1451  105
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 4728 1451  106
to the highest incident energy.                                   4728 1451  107
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:4728 1451  108
                                                                  4728 1451  109
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section: nuclear +          4728 1451  110
             interference terms                                   4728 1451  111
                                                                  4728 1451  112
Obtained by integrating the "nuclear-plus-interference" angular   4728 1451  113
distributions of MF=6.  Note that because of the interference     4728 1451  114
effect, the tabulations in both MF=6 and MF=3 can be negative at  4728 1451  115
some energies and angles.                                         4728 1451  116
                                                                  4728 1451  117
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            4728 1451  118
                                                                  4728 1451  119
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    4728 1451  120
                                                                  4728 1451  121
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        4728 1451  122
                                                                  4728 1451  123
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  4728 1451  124
                                                                  4728 1451  125
- MT5      : (p,anything) cross section                           4728 1451  126
                                                                  4728 1451  127
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   4728 1451  128
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        4728 1451  129
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     4728 1451  130
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         4728 1451  131
sections.                                                         4728 1451  132
                                                                  4728 1451  133
- MT16     : (p,2n) cross section                                 4728 1451  134
- MT17     : (p,3n) cross section                                 4728 1451  135
- MT22     : (p,na) cross section                                 4728 1451  136
- MT28     : (p,np) cross section                                 4728 1451  137
- MT51-90  : (p,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      4728 1451  138
- MT91     : (p,n') continuum cross section                       4728 1451  139
- MT102    : (p,gamma) cross section                              4728 1451  140
- MT103    : (p,p) cross section                                  4728 1451  141
- MT104    : (p,d) cross section                                  4728 1451  142
- MT105    : (p,t) cross section                                  4728 1451  143
- MT106    : (p,h) cross section                                  4728 1451  144
- MT107    : (p,a) cross section                                  4728 1451  145
- MT600-610: (p,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       4728 1451  146
- MT649    : (p,p) continuum cross section                        4728 1451  147
- MT650-655: (p,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        4728 1451  148
- MT699    : (p,d) continuum cross section                        4728 1451  149
- MT700-705: (p,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        4728 1451  150
- MT749    : (p,t) continuum cross section                        4728 1451  151
- MT750-755: (p,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        4728 1451  152
- MT799    : (p,h) continuum cross section                        4728 1451  153
- MT800-810: (p,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       4728 1451  154
- MT849    : (p,a) continuum cross section                        4728 1451  155
                                                                  4728 1451  156
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     4728 1451  157
                                                                  4728 1451  158
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     4728 1451  159
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   4728 1451  160
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  4728 1451  161
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             4728 1451  162
All data are generated with TALYS.                                4728 1451  163
                                                                  4728 1451  164
- MT5      : (p,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   4728 1451  165
                                                                  4728 1451  166
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      4728 1451  167
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   4728 1451  168
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   4728 1451  169
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are4728 1451  170
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   4728 1451  171
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  4728 1451  172
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              4728 1451  173
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 4728 1451  174
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  4728 1451  175
For each residual product:                                        4728 1451  176
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               4728 1451  177
- the recoil                                                      4728 1451  178
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         4728 1451  179
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     4728 1451  180
sections.                                                         4728 1451  181
                                                                  4728 1451  182
- MT16     : (p,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     4728 1451  183
                                                                  4728 1451  184
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  4728 1451  185
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 4728 1451  186
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          4728 1451  187
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       4728 1451  188
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 4728 1451  189
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     4728 1451  190
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  4728 1451  191
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      4728 1451  192
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         4728 1451  193
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             4728 1451  194
                                                                  4728 1451  195
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   4728 1451  196
followed:                                                         4728 1451  197
                                                                  4728 1451  198
- MT17 : (p,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         4728 1451  199
- MT22 : (p,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         4728 1451  200
- MT28 : (p,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         4728 1451  201
- MT91 : (p,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     4728 1451  202
- MT649: (p,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     4728 1451  203
- MT699: (p,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     4728 1451  204
- MT749: (p,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     4728 1451  205
- MT809: (p,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     4728 1451  206
- MT849: (p,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     4728 1451  207
                                                                  4728 1451  208
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 4728 1451  209
                                                                  4728 1451  210
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    4728 1451  211
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          4728 1451  212
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     4728 1451  213
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          4728 1451  214
                                                                  4728 1451  215
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  4728 1451  216
                                                                  4728 1451  217
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     4728 1451  218
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    4728 1451  219
as isomer.                                                        4728 1451  220
                                                                  4728 1451  221
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 4728 1451  222
                                                                  4728 1451  223
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        4728 1451  224
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    4728 1451  225
as isomer.                                                        4728 1451  226
                                                                  4728 1451  227
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 4728 1451  228
                                                                  4728 1451  229
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  4728 1451  230
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     4728 1451  231
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    4728 1451  232
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   4728 1451  233
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  4728 1451  234
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                4728 1451  235
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      4728 1451  236
   same reaction channel between different energies)              4728 1451  237
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      4728 1451  238
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               4728 1451  239
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      4728 1451  240
   different reaction channels for different energies)            4728 1451  241
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        4728 1451  242
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              4728 1451  243
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  4728 1451  244
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       4728 1451  245
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     4728 1451  246
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  4728 1451  247
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     4728 1451  248
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     4728 1451  249
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     4728 1451  250
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   4728 1451  251
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   4728 1451  252
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  4728 1451  253
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   4728 1451  254
                                                                  4728 1451  255
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      4728 1451  256
                                                                  4728 1451  257
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  4728 1451  258
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             4728 1451  259
                                                                  4728 1451  260
